as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of sheep, and the denominator represents the number of goats.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $10:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 10}{1\\times 10}=\\frac{30}{10}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Manuel has $30$ sheep and $10$ goats. So, the total number of animals in the herd is \n\n$$\n30+10=40.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19618e12-debd-5b4e-9bf1-429e65d1a0bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330167} {:answer/id #uuid "5a4d2098-760f-5acc-84b4-40651c95e415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330758} {:answer/id #uuid "5bdcbebb-943f-5a2c-92b4-c3828824f1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330771} {:answer/id #uuid "7d4abe4a-1493-5b17-9061-c2a59e27d5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331053} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf4ef6e-5e9b-5fbd-8000-7085f8f93e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d4abe4a-1493-5b17-9061-c2a59e27d5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331053} :answer-field/id #uuid "cecfd35c-e905-59a9-a911-bac01e2f48fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9aff327a-3ab5-5bdb-b2ab-437fac7b7394" :question/math-academy-id "q-59895" :question/problem "There are $15$ students in a class, and $\\frac{2}{5}$ of them wear glasses. How many students **do not** wear glasses?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of students who wear glasses to the total number of students is $\\frac{2}{5}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of students who wear glasses, and the denominator represents the total number of students.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $15$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 3}{5\\times 3}=\\frac{6}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $6$ students who wear glasses. \n\nSo the number of students who don't wear glasses is\n\n$$\n15-6=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f71bb97-ece8-546e-a7a7-8359437ebda2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516320} {:answer/id #uuid "701eba46-6034-5191-b8c0-f4010b286be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516363} {:answer/id #uuid "70b5c337-134d-5b23-8234-a694bfeab0ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516365} {:answer/id #uuid "bff2951a-541e-5f2c-b035-f5b17ef671ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516519} {:answer/id #uuid "dc72bee6-483f-5536-ad4b-5f542ab698ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70b5c337-134d-5b23-8234-a694bfeab0ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516365} :answer-field/id #uuid "c50e1709-fb35-5c84-a6d5-30b4b5bd93b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bea17d69-eb40-57fe-baa2-90eb85105abf" :question/math-academy-id "q-60197" :question/problem "In an electronics store, the ratio of the number of cell phones to the total number of gadgets sold (cell phones and computers) is $\\frac{8}{11}.$ If $16$ cell phones were sold in a week, how many computers were sold?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of the number of cell phones sold to the number of gadgets (cell phones and computers) sold is $\\frac{8}{11}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of cell phones sold and the denominator represents the number of cell phones and computers sold.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $16$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{8\\times 2}{11\\times 2}=\\frac{16}{22}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number of cell phones and computers sold that week was $22.$ Of this amount, the number of computers sold was\n\n$$\n22-16=6.\n$$"}]}
